# 中频词汇 List07
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2024恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List07核心词汇

{{extraordinary}}{/ɪkˈstrɔːdnri/}{非凡的；特别的}{The discovery was an extraordinary achievement for science.}}
{{extreme}}{/ɪkˈstriːm/}{极端的；极度的}{Extreme poverty affects millions of people worldwide.}}
{{fabric}}{/ˈfæbrɪk/}{织物；结构}{The social fabric of the community was torn apart by conflict.}}
{{fade}}{/feɪd/}{褪色；消退}{Interest in the topic has gradually faded over time.}}
{{failure}}{/ˈfeɪljər/}{失败；故障}{The project ended in failure due to poor planning.}}
{{fantasy}}{/ˈfæntəsi/}{幻想；想象}{The line between reality and fantasy is often blurred.}}
{{fatal}}{/ˈfeɪtl/}{致命的；灾难性的}{The flaw in the design proved fatal to the project.}}
{{feasible}}{/ˈfiːzəbl/}{可行的；可能的}{The proposed solution is technically feasible and cost-effective.}}
{{fierce}}{/fɪəs/}{激烈的；凶猛的}{Competition for the scholarship is fierce.}}
{{fiscal}}{/ˈfɪskl/}{财政的；国库的}{The government announced new fiscal measures to curb inflation.}}
{{flaw}}{/flɔː/}{缺陷；瑕疵}{The study was criticized for a fundamental flaw in its methodology.}}
{{flee}}{/fliː/}{逃跑；逃离}{Many families fled the area ahead of the hurricane.}}
{{flourish}}{/ˈflʌrɪʃ/}{繁荣；兴旺}{Art and culture flourished during the Renaissance.}}
{{forecast}}{/ˈfɔːkɑːst/}{预测；预报}{Analysts forecast a slowdown in economic growth.}}
{{forge}}{/fɔːdʒ/}{锻造；伪造}{The two countries forged a new trade agreement.}}
{{formal}}{/ˈfɔːml/}{正式的；正规的}{A formal announcement will be made tomorrow.}}
{{format}}{/ˈfɔːmæt/}{格式；版式}{The data is available in digital format.}}
{{former}}{/ˈfɔːmər/}{以前的；前者}{The former CEO now serves as an advisor.}}
{{foster}}{/ˈfɒstər/}{培养；促进}{The program fosters creativity and critical thinking.}}
{{fraction}}{/ˈfrækʃn/}{分数；一小部分}{Only a fraction of applicants are accepted into the program.}}
{{fragile}}{/ˈfrædʒaɪl/}{脆弱的；易碎的}{The peace agreement remains fragile.}}
{{framework}}{/ˈfreɪmwɜːk/}{框架；结构}{The legal framework needs to be updated for the digital age.}}
{{friction}}{/ˈfrɪkʃn/}{摩擦；冲突}{There was friction between the two departments over resources.}}
{{fulfill}}{/fʊlˈfɪl/}{实现；履行}{The organization fulfilled its promise to the community.}}
{{fundamental}}{/ˌfʌndəˈmentl/}{基本的；根本的}{The theory challenged fundamental assumptions in physics.}}
{{gang}}{/ɡæŋ/}{一帮；一伙}{A gang of thieves was arrested by the police.}}
{{gap}}{/ɡæp/}{差距；缺口}{The gap between rich and poor continues to widen.}}
{{gather}}{/ˈɡæðər/}{收集；聚集}{The team gathered data from over 1,000 participants.}}
{{genuine}}{/ˈdʒenjuɪn/}{真正的；真诚的}{She showed genuine concern for her students' well-being.}}
{{gesture}}{/ˈdʒestʃər/}{手势；姿态}{The donation was a generous gesture of goodwill.}}
